            ”
          %p
            Discussion for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+M-theory"} bosonic M-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Keith+Glennon"}> Keith Glennon
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+West"} Peter West
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mn 27
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_{27}
                  as a symmetry of closed bosonic strings and branes
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08649"}> arXiv:2409.08649
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Keith+Glennon"}> Keith Glennon
                \:
                %em Bosonic M-Theory From a Kac-Moody Algebra Perspective
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.03000"}> arXiv:2501.03000
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#further_details Further details
          %p
            A careful discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Moody+group"} Kac-Moody
            U-duality groups is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arjan+Keurentjes"}> Arjan Keurentjes
                ,
                %em The topology of U-duality (sub-)groups
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0309106"}> arXiv:hep-th/0309106
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arjan+Keurentjes"}> Arjan Keurentjes
                ,
                %em U-duality (sub-)groups and their topology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0312134"}> arXiv:hep-th/0312134
                )
          %p
            A discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+complex+geometry"} generalized complex geometry
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+generalized+complex+geometry"} exceptional generalized complex geometry
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Paulo Pires Pacheco,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Waldram"} Daniel Waldram
                %em M-theory, exceptional generalised geometry and superpotentials
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0804.1362"}> arXiv:0804.1362
                )
            %li
              %p
                Nicholas Houston,
                %em Supergravity and Generalized Geometry
                Thesis (2010) (
                %a{:href => "https://workspace.imperial.ac.uk/theoreticalphysics/Public/MSc/Dissertations/2010/Nicholas%20Houston%20Dissertation.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            General discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Moody+groups"} Kac-Moody groups
            arising in this context is for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              Philipp Fleig,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Axel+Kleinschmidt"} Axel Kleinschmidt
              %em Eisenstein series for infinite-dimensional U-duality groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1204.3043"}> arXiv:1204.3043
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Kleinschmidt12.pdf", :title => "slides"} slides
          %h3#relation_to_automorphic_forms Relation to automorphic forms
          %p
            String theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+functions"} partition functions
            as
